00:24:51.190 --> 00:24:53.500
How is it? Is it good?

00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:57.300
Of course it has to be.

00:24:58.070 --> 00:24:59.700
It's the first dish you've ever made.

00:24:59.770 --> 00:25:01.610
Really? That's a relief.

00:25:07.840 --> 00:25:10.550
Right. For your first time cooking...

00:25:11.380 --> 00:25:12.980
It tastes about how you'd expect.

00:25:14.750 --> 00:25:18.020
But what's the occasion? You've never cooked in your life.

00:25:19.920 --> 00:25:22.230
You brought so much. Just how much curry did you make?

00:25:23.760 --> 00:25:27.930
Seriously, who were you planning to eat all this with?

00:25:28.500 --> 00:25:30.829
You're supposed to make a lot of curry at once.

00:25:30.830 --> 00:25:35.010
They say it tastes better over the next couple of days.

00:25:36.540 --> 00:25:37.540
That's true.

00:25:39.210 --> 00:25:41.780
So it'll taste better tomorrow, right?

00:25:43.610 --> 00:25:44.610
What?

00:25:52.460 --> 00:25:53.960
- Much better. - Sorry?

00:25:54.020 --> 00:25:56.230
I'm saying it'll be even tastier.

00:25:56.960 --> 00:25:57.960
Right?

00:25:58.300 --> 00:26:00.160
- Give me some more. - Should I?

00:26:00.730 --> 00:26:03.730
But I wonder who would've told you that.

00:26:08.940 --> 00:26:10.670
- Dad. - Yes?

00:26:10.770 --> 00:26:12.080
I'm seeing someone...

00:26:13.540 --> 00:26:15.110
- What? - What?

00:26:15.550 --> 00:26:16.550
What did you say?

00:26:17.150 --> 00:26:18.150
What?

00:26:22.090 --> 00:26:23.350
- What? - What?

00:26:23.420 --> 00:26:24.420
What was it?

00:26:25.990 --> 00:26:28.330
I'm seeing someone.

00:26:30.790 --> 00:26:33.730
I know the timing is a little weird, but...

00:26:44.740 --> 00:26:46.040
Are you okay with that?

00:26:48.350 --> 00:26:49.650
Of course I am.

00:26:50.550 --> 00:26:52.180
Liking someone...

00:26:53.180 --> 00:26:54.620
is a true blessing.

00:26:57.150 --> 00:26:58.120
Congratulations.

00:26:59.160 --> 00:27:00.160
Thank you.

00:27:00.161 --> 00:27:02.530
This is how you come clean? How anticlimactic.

00:27:03.790 --> 00:27:05.800
I should have held onto that card a little longer.

00:27:06.360 --> 00:27:07.360
What a shame.

00:27:12.570 --> 00:27:13.570
A big shame.

00:27:36.130 --> 00:27:37.390
You still not done unpacking?

00:27:38.900 --> 00:27:40.030
I'm all done.

00:27:40.660 --> 00:27:41.660
I'm...

00:27:42.170 --> 00:27:43.230
done too.

00:27:45.340 --> 00:27:46.340
I see.

00:27:48.070 --> 00:27:49.440
A little bare, isn't it?

00:27:52.610 --> 00:27:54.280
You should put up some posters of idols or something.

00:27:56.210 --> 00:27:57.580
And if you need anything, just let me know.

00:27:59.850 --> 00:28:00.920
I don't.

00:28:01.650 --> 00:28:02.920
Come on, what kind of son are you?

00:28:05.090 --> 00:28:07.290
You're supposed to whine and ask your dad to buy you stuff.

00:28:12.930 --> 00:28:13.960
Whine?

00:28:19.700 --> 00:28:22.210
Let me spoil you a little.

00:28:27.640 --> 00:28:28.780
Spoil me?

00:28:34.220 --> 00:28:35.550
I just want us to be closer.

00:28:37.420 --> 00:28:38.420
Okay.

00:28:49.830 --> 00:28:51.130
Finish up.

00:28:55.000 --> 00:28:56.010
Daniel.

00:28:59.540 --> 00:29:02.250
My girlfriend.

00:29:04.680 --> 00:29:06.380
Would it be okay if I invited her over?

00:29:13.620 --> 00:29:15.590
I want you...

00:29:17.390 --> 00:29:20.560
to get along with my girlfriend.

00:29:29.710 --> 00:29:30.740
Okay.

00:29:31.810 --> 00:29:32.810
Really?

00:29:34.080 --> 00:29:35.280
If you're happy,

00:29:36.610 --> 00:29:37.680
then I'm happy too.

00:30:14.650 --> 00:30:15.890
Your hair dye...

00:30:17.290 --> 00:30:19.960
Yes, I stopped halfway through dyeing it.

00:30:20.490 --> 00:30:21.520
Just these parts.

00:30:22.460 --> 00:30:23.590
It looks weird, right?

00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:30.400
- Let me see your phone. - What?

00:30:30.900 --> 00:30:32.300
Why?

00:30:45.110 --> 00:30:49.050
See? I knew it. "Guide?" Seriously?

00:30:50.020 --> 00:30:51.220
I have a name, you know.

00:30:54.460 --> 00:30:57.160
(Ja Yeong)

00:31:02.470 --> 00:31:03.930
Then what do you have me saved as?

00:31:09.440 --> 00:31:12.910
(Jin Ho)

00:31:21.550 --> 00:31:22.750
All right, let's hear it.

00:31:25.150 --> 00:31:26.260
Hear what?

00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:29.390
Your excuse for not calling me for days...

00:31:29.460 --> 00:31:30.830
after we spent the night together.

00:31:35.400 --> 00:31:36.400
The truth is,

00:31:38.500 --> 00:31:39.700
it made me terrified.

00:31:42.370 --> 00:31:43.370
Of what?

00:31:45.540 --> 00:31:47.340
The thought of people finding out about my feelings...

00:31:48.080 --> 00:31:49.680
for you.

00:31:55.550 --> 00:31:57.290
- So? - But now...

00:31:58.860 --> 00:32:00.560
you've given me courage.

00:32:01.660 --> 00:32:03.030
So I've made up my mind, just now.

00:32:03.530 --> 00:32:05.530
No one else is going to live my life for me.

00:32:05.960 --> 00:32:06.960
So...

00:32:07.260 --> 00:32:09.030
I guess I have to find my own happiness.

00:32:09.700 --> 00:32:10.700
Right?

00:32:14.200 --> 00:32:17.310
From now on, Ja Yeong, I'm not going to care what anyone else thinks.

00:32:20.410 --> 00:32:21.410
Sir?

00:32:22.910 --> 00:32:24.380
- Hey. - Sir.

00:32:24.450 --> 00:32:26.820
- Hi. - What brings you here?

00:32:27.480 --> 00:32:28.520
Me? Oh, you know.

00:32:30.420 --> 00:32:32.060
It's a nice day, so I just came out for a walk.

00:32:33.260 --> 00:32:36.560
- With her? - No, I don't know her.

00:32:38.360 --> 00:32:41.530
- What about you? - We're promoting the Care Program.

00:32:41.830 --> 00:32:43.170
Everyone else is over there.

00:32:43.670 --> 00:32:46.540
- The Care Program? - Yes. You should come say hi.

00:32:46.600 --> 00:32:48.470
- Should I? - Yes.

00:32:49.170 --> 00:32:50.210
This way.

00:32:50.910 --> 00:32:52.610
- I'm sorry. - Where are you...

00:32:53.440 --> 00:32:54.510
It's our director.

00:32:55.510 --> 00:32:58.280
- Hello, sir. - Hey. It's been a while.

00:33:10.990 --> 00:33:12.400
Who are you?

00:33:14.160 --> 00:33:16.930
A friend of mine is going on a trip and asked me to watch her,

00:33:17.000 --> 00:33:18.230
so I brought her over this morning.

00:33:18.840 --> 00:33:19.870
Which friend?

00:33:21.440 --> 00:33:22.770
It's... You know.

00:33:23.370 --> 00:33:27.140
The one who moved to Bundang or Dongtan. You don't know him?

00:33:27.440 --> 00:33:28.440
I'm sure you do.

00:33:30.350 --> 00:33:31.350
I don't.

00:33:31.850 --> 00:33:36.250
- Hey, you're handsome. - Jun Seo, she's a girl.

00:33:37.790 --> 00:33:39.760
My bad. I mean, you're pretty.

00:33:41.790 --> 00:33:44.630
Seeing this little one reminds me of raising you and Jun Kyung.

00:33:45.190 --> 00:33:48.060
Feeding you on time, cleaning up after you, and playing with you.

00:33:48.260 --> 00:33:50.930
You know, those were the most fun times of my life.

00:33:51.970 --> 00:33:55.510
Hey. This guy Jun Kyung's seeing, what's he like?

00:33:55.670 --> 00:33:56.740
Is he someone I know?

00:33:58.070 --> 00:33:59.810
I've seen him once.

00:34:00.280 --> 00:34:01.540
But I don't know if that counts as "knowing" him.

00:34:02.910 --> 00:34:03.950
Well...

00:34:05.250 --> 00:34:06.550
I'm sure he's a good guy.

00:34:07.150 --> 00:34:08.420
What do you mean by "I'm sure?"

00:34:09.050 --> 00:34:10.950
He must be, if he's willing to date Jun Kyung.

00:34:11.720 --> 00:34:12.690
That's true.

00:34:14.920 --> 00:34:17.560
- What's her name again? - What? Bom.

00:34:18.230 --> 00:34:19.900
- Bom. - Bom.

00:34:33.140 --> 00:34:34.340
It's an honour to meet you.

00:34:35.480 --> 00:34:36.950
My name is Ju Do Hyun.

00:34:44.550 --> 00:34:46.160
Thank you for suggesting we meet here.

00:34:49.090 --> 00:34:50.930
Of course. It's only right.

00:34:56.400 --> 00:34:57.930
I wanted to pay my respects.

00:35:06.180 --> 00:35:07.410
This is unexpected.

00:35:09.510 --> 00:35:11.580
This is where the person they loved is laid to rest,

00:35:13.450 --> 00:35:14.820
but they don't seem all that sad.

00:35:16.390 --> 00:35:17.550
Everyone's smiling.

00:35:22.290 --> 00:35:24.130
I think enough time has passed.

00:35:25.800 --> 00:35:26.900
So now,

00:35:27.760 --> 00:35:28.970
when they miss them...

00:35:30.900 --> 00:35:32.200
and want to see them,

00:35:35.910 --> 00:35:37.510
they can come here with happy hearts.

00:35:45.920 --> 00:35:46.920
Is it this nice...

00:35:46.980 --> 00:35:47.980
so that we'll visit often?

00:35:59.460 --> 00:36:02.330
I'm okay, but it's my dad I'm worried about.

00:36:10.610 --> 00:36:12.980
Hurrah!

00:36:14.440 --> 00:36:16.780
Goodness. Hurrah!

00:36:20.220 --> 00:36:21.320
Look, it's Mommy!

00:36:21.780 --> 00:36:25.420
It's Mommy! Look, it's Mommy!

00:36:28.590 --> 00:36:29.890
Hey, what time is it over there?

00:36:30.330 --> 00:36:32.960
There's only a one-hour difference in Hong Kong.

00:36:33.060 --> 00:36:35.800
One hour. I wouldn't know. I've never been abroad.

00:36:36.600 --> 00:36:37.930
How's our little Bom doing?

00:36:38.070 --> 00:36:42.610
I was just playing with her. She's hopping around so cutely.

00:36:44.040 --> 00:36:45.470
I miss you, Bom.

00:36:45.880 --> 00:36:48.810
- I'll see you in two days. - I miss you too.

00:36:50.010 --> 00:36:51.750
I miss you too, Jin Ho.

00:36:58.150 --> 00:37:03.390
I was so scared this kind of laser treatment would hurt,

00:37:04.060 --> 00:37:05.460
but it doesn't hurt one bit.

00:37:05.800 --> 00:37:06.900
See? I told you.

00:37:07.530 --> 00:37:09.229
Jun Kyung, you should get it too while you're here.

00:37:09.230 --> 00:37:10.230
Right?

00:37:10.370 --> 00:37:14.170
No husband, kids, or mother-in-law.

00:37:14.340 --> 00:37:16.310
She's got none of the stress that causes all those skin problems.

00:37:17.140 --> 00:37:18.710
It's all about preventative care.

00:37:19.040 --> 00:37:21.680
He's probably too old for something like this, right?

00:37:22.080 --> 00:37:24.280
Of course. He's too busy with tutoring and extracurriculars.

00:37:24.850 --> 00:37:26.950
Darn, what would be a good gift?

00:37:27.220 --> 00:37:30.590
You're the mom of an eighth grader. Give me an idea.

00:37:31.250 --> 00:37:34.990
- You're really thinking about this. - I can't go empty-handed, can I?

00:37:35.060 --> 00:37:37.790
Just do what you always do. Isn't cash always king with you?

00:37:37.890 --> 00:37:42.300
She hates wasting time and emotion, so she just throws money at things.

00:37:42.400 --> 00:37:44.400
Whatever. You can't just give a kid money.

00:37:44.470 --> 00:37:49.310
Says the one who gave my daughters cash for their fourth birthday.

00:37:49.440 --> 00:37:53.410
What's with the parent act? Do you really care what he thinks?

00:37:53.580 --> 00:37:55.579
A good impression is impossible.

00:37:55.580 --> 00:37:57.880
But I don't have to be the worst, do I?

00:37:58.450 --> 00:38:00.480
What do you think? He'd like this, right?

00:38:02.020 --> 00:38:05.690
You dare to guess what a middle schooler finds stylish?

00:38:07.190 --> 00:38:10.090
Hey, this is it, right? This is the one.

00:38:10.560 --> 00:38:14.460
All their classes are on that now. Every kid's got one.

00:38:15.230 --> 00:38:16.700
Since when?

00:38:17.700 --> 00:38:18.700
All done.

00:38:19.100 --> 00:38:22.710
Already? Give me a mirror.

00:38:26.940 --> 00:38:28.440
Oh, my gosh.

00:38:29.210 --> 00:38:30.410
- Hey. - What?

00:38:30.480 --> 00:38:33.180
- My skin looks so bright. - Right.

00:38:34.420 --> 00:38:35.420
Yes?

00:38:37.990 --> 00:38:40.590
- Are you Ju Do Hyun? - Yes, that's me.

00:38:41.360 --> 00:38:43.030
- Can I get your signature, please? - Right.

00:38:50.600 --> 00:38:51.600
Gosh.

00:38:53.170 --> 00:38:56.040
- How did you think of such a gift? - Is it okay?

00:38:57.210 --> 00:38:59.840
I went back and forth on it. Do you think Daniel will like it?

00:38:59.910 --> 00:39:01.480
He'll love it, of course.

00:39:02.080 --> 00:39:04.050
He would never even dream of a gift like this.

00:39:04.250 --> 00:39:08.280
So, who's the lucky guy that gets to live in this house?

00:39:08.620 --> 00:39:10.850
Look forward to finding out.

00:39:21.230 --> 00:39:22.870
It feels so nice and cool out here. This is great.

00:39:27.140 --> 00:39:28.540
They look happy.

00:39:45.420 --> 00:39:48.060
- Yes. - May I come in?

00:39:48.420 --> 00:39:49.430
Come on in.

00:39:51.960 --> 00:39:53.100
All right, I got it.

00:39:55.160 --> 00:39:56.170
Okay.

00:39:57.230 --> 00:40:00.670
- I'll get going now. - You shouldn't have... All right.

00:40:05.470 --> 00:40:06.480
Have a seat.

00:40:14.480 --> 00:40:15.520
Any idea why I called you in?

00:40:18.790 --> 00:40:19.760
I'm not sure, sir.

00:40:22.060 --> 00:40:23.060
Want a drink?

00:40:23.560 --> 00:40:24.560
Excuse me?

00:40:27.460 --> 00:40:29.769
She should be focused on her work.

00:40:29.770 --> 00:40:32.070
And yet, she never forgets things like this.

00:40:32.570 --> 00:40:35.170
Should I consider this an effort too?

00:40:38.540 --> 00:40:39.810
Let's see.

00:40:47.720 --> 00:40:50.050
So, you resubmitted your assignment?

00:40:50.650 --> 00:40:51.790
Yes.

00:40:52.120 --> 00:40:53.790
Why'd you do that?

00:40:55.590 --> 00:40:57.960
Were you annoyed because I chewed you out?

00:40:58.190 --> 00:40:59.460
No. That's not it at all.

00:40:59.530 --> 00:41:01.830
If that's not it, there's no reason you would've resubmitted.

00:41:01.900 --> 00:41:03.730
The deadline passed, and your grade has already been finalized.

00:41:03.830 --> 00:41:05.000
It was completely pointless.

00:41:08.070 --> 00:41:09.070
It's just...

00:41:10.170 --> 00:41:13.610
I wanted to know what it feels like to really put in the effort.

00:41:17.210 --> 00:41:18.210
Effort?

00:41:21.580 --> 00:41:25.350
Right, your undergraduate major was astronomy, wasn't it?

00:41:25.750 --> 00:41:26.760
Yes.

00:41:28.060 --> 00:41:29.290
That must be it.

00:41:30.090 --> 00:41:31.160
You're a bit of an idealist.

00:41:34.060 --> 00:41:35.060
Thank you.

00:41:36.500 --> 00:41:37.500
How would you like an internship?

00:41:39.030 --> 00:41:40.040
What?

00:41:40.500 --> 00:41:44.710
A former student at JCBC needs a media studies research intern,

00:41:44.840 --> 00:41:46.180
and they asked me to recommend someone.

00:41:46.740 --> 00:41:49.580
Hyo Jung was just here asking about that, actually.

00:41:49.980 --> 00:41:51.510
It's funny, you know?

00:41:51.810 --> 00:41:55.620
I try to be fair, but you can only do so much. Right?

00:41:57.690 --> 00:42:01.160
Your attitude is much more endearing than this kind of thing.

00:42:09.570 --> 00:42:10.870
So, you in or out?

00:42:14.470 --> 00:42:18.240
Is the water temperature okay? Yes? You like it? You do!

00:42:18.770 --> 00:42:20.880
You little rascal. You're so cute.

00:42:27.380 --> 00:42:28.949
- Yes? - Dad,

00:42:28.950 --> 00:42:31.420
I might get a research internship at a TV station.

00:42:31.720 --> 00:42:33.320
- A research intern? - Yes.

00:42:33.390 --> 00:42:35.060
Gosh, that sounds really impressive.

00:42:35.120 --> 00:42:37.930
My professor is recommending me over all the grad and PhD students!

00:42:38.290 --> 00:42:42.160
That's my boy! Incredible! Congratulations!

00:42:42.360 --> 00:42:43.370
I'm going to be a little late tonight.

00:42:43.530 --> 00:42:45.100
Sure. Go have a drink with your friends.

00:42:45.170 --> 00:42:46.970
I've got to step out myself, so don't worry about it.

00:42:47.040 --> 00:42:48.340
I might not even come home tonight.

00:42:48.540 --> 00:42:52.370
Not coming home? Fine. Go out with your friends. Just stay out.

00:42:52.440 --> 00:42:54.410
- Okay. - Hey, Dad.

00:42:55.440 --> 00:42:56.450
I love you.

00:43:04.490 --> 00:43:08.220
Bom, where'd you go? There she is.

00:43:08.290 --> 00:43:11.660
Come here. That's it. There we go.

00:43:13.000 --> 00:43:14.300
Let's get you all finished up.

00:43:14.930 --> 00:43:16.230
There we go. So cute.

00:43:16.570 --> 00:43:17.570
For real?

00:43:24.910 --> 00:43:26.780
That's incredible, Seo Jun Seo!

00:43:27.010 --> 00:43:29.810
This is seriously all thanks to you, so I'm paying for everything.

00:43:29.910 --> 00:43:32.780
What did I tell you? I said you're not pathetic, right?

00:43:33.280 --> 00:43:34.780
I told you you're awesome just the way you are, didn't I?

00:43:35.990 --> 00:43:37.650
Those are the facts.

00:43:37.720 --> 00:43:38.720
Okay.

00:43:38.721 --> 00:43:41.460
From pork cutlet, jjolmyeon, sushi, to tteokbokki. I'm buying, okay?

00:43:42.320 --> 00:43:43.330
Thank you!

00:43:49.570 --> 00:43:53.270
All right! I'm officially a working man!

00:44:06.520 --> 00:44:08.520
Hi.

00:44:12.590 --> 00:44:13.560
Hey. You're here.

00:44:20.860 --> 00:44:22.000
A half-moon betta.

00:44:23.830 --> 00:44:24.830
Gosh.

00:44:25.770 --> 00:44:27.270
It looks so mysterious.

00:44:28.070 --> 00:44:29.740
But it looks a little lonely all by itself.

00:44:29.810 --> 00:44:32.010
Should we get another one to be its friend?

00:44:32.910 --> 00:44:36.080
This species isn't social, so they're usually kept alone.

00:44:39.250 --> 00:44:40.250
In that case...

00:44:41.920 --> 00:44:43.720
You can be its friend then, Daniel.

00:44:48.860 --> 00:44:53.030
Once it fully adjusts to the tank, it'll come to the surface for food,

00:44:53.300 --> 00:44:55.530
and they're as playful as puppies, so people call them "water dogs."

00:44:59.500 --> 00:45:00.570
Pretty, isn't it?

00:45:04.570 --> 00:45:06.010
Like I said, he's shy with new people.

00:45:09.280 --> 00:45:11.610
You don't have to be shy with a fish, man.

00:45:13.750 --> 00:45:15.120
Here, look.

00:45:18.420 --> 00:45:21.490
Ja Yeong, it's time to come back to reality.

00:45:24.460 --> 00:45:26.400
But I like this reality much better.

00:45:28.430 --> 00:45:30.030
Bom, have you been a good girl?

00:45:30.600 --> 00:45:32.030
Did you have fun playing with him?

00:45:32.530 --> 00:45:33.540
It must have been tough.

00:45:33.740 --> 00:45:36.910
Yes, it was torture. I was dying for some kimchi stew.

00:45:37.110 --> 00:45:39.010
What? Kimchi stew?

00:45:40.280 --> 00:45:43.210
I know this amazing place for kimchi stew.

00:45:45.180 --> 00:45:46.180
Let's go.

00:45:48.280 --> 00:45:49.280
Ja Yeong, come on in.

00:45:51.850 --> 00:45:52.860
It's all right.

00:45:56.260 --> 00:45:59.730
Goodness. This is so nice.

00:46:00.260 --> 00:46:01.360
It's nothing special.

00:46:02.460 --> 00:46:04.030
My son said he's coming home late tonight.

00:46:05.230 --> 00:46:06.240
He might not even make it home.

00:46:08.540 --> 00:46:10.910
As a welcome-home present, I'll make you kimchi stew.

00:46:11.010 --> 00:46:13.040
I brought a gift too.

00:46:13.510 --> 00:46:15.610
- A gift? - Matching T-shirts.

00:46:15.940 --> 00:46:16.950
Matching T-shirts?

00:46:19.250 --> 00:46:20.250
But...

00:46:21.250 --> 00:46:23.820
- Are you sure it's okay to come in? - It's fine.

00:46:26.490 --> 00:46:29.460
Ja Yeong, wait just a second. Hold on.

00:46:35.000 --> 00:46:36.000
For crying out loud.

00:47:18.040 --> 00:47:19.040
Man.

00:47:19.610 --> 00:47:20.940
(Eternal Love)

00:47:27.750 --> 00:47:29.050
Is practice still not over?

00:47:30.150 --> 00:47:31.150
What's taking so long?

00:47:34.960 --> 00:47:36.060
Wait a minute.

00:47:38.860 --> 00:47:39.860
Gosh.

00:47:42.300 --> 00:47:43.470
Hey, Auntie.

00:47:43.530 --> 00:47:46.340
Hey. I have an errand in your neighbourhood,

00:47:46.400 --> 00:47:47.870
so let me bring some young radish kimchi over.

00:47:48.070 --> 00:47:50.110
You know how your dad loves it.

00:47:50.170 --> 00:47:52.840
I'm stopping by after my errand. You're home, aren't you?

00:47:52.940 --> 00:47:54.680
Your dad's not answering his phone.

00:47:55.380 --> 00:47:57.080
I'm actually out right now.

00:47:57.680 --> 00:47:59.450
Dad said he was going out soon too.

00:47:59.780 --> 00:48:00.850
Really?

00:48:01.380 --> 00:48:03.850
Then what am I supposed to do with all this?

00:48:16.730 --> 00:48:17.970
Daniel, what do you like to do?

00:48:19.600 --> 00:48:20.600
You know, hobbies and stuff.

00:48:24.910 --> 00:48:25.910
Why?

00:48:30.280 --> 00:48:31.280
Just curious.

00:48:33.420 --> 00:48:34.420
I don't have any.

00:48:38.390 --> 00:48:40.720
You like skateboarding, don't you?

00:48:40.990 --> 00:48:43.090
You're always watching videos and practising tricks.

00:48:44.060 --> 00:48:47.000
And he takes after me, so he loves music too.

00:48:47.360 --> 00:48:48.500
But our tastes are a little different.

00:48:48.860 --> 00:48:49.870
He's strictly into hip-hop.

00:48:59.110 --> 00:49:00.840
Want some of this? It's really delicious.

00:49:01.280 --> 00:49:04.550
- No, I'm good. - I feel bad eating this alone.

00:49:04.680 --> 00:49:05.950
No, that's not...

00:49:09.580 --> 00:49:10.590
Are you okay?

00:49:10.920 --> 00:49:11.920
Yes.

00:49:12.450 --> 00:49:13.460
Are you okay?

00:49:14.160 --> 00:49:15.160
I'm fine.

00:49:16.690 --> 00:49:18.090
I'm sorry, Dad.

00:49:26.340 --> 00:49:27.870
It's okay. It was just an accident.

00:49:38.880 --> 00:49:39.880
Yes?

00:49:48.990 --> 00:49:50.730
I'm sorry, Jun Kyung.

00:49:51.430 --> 00:49:52.430
For what?

00:49:53.430 --> 00:49:56.630
I feel like I might have made things unnecessarily awkward.

00:49:58.170 --> 00:50:01.400
If anyone was uncomfortable, it was Daniel, not me. Don't worry.

00:50:05.240 --> 00:50:07.380
- So you were worried for nothing. - Yes.

00:50:07.440 --> 00:50:08.440
It's fine.

00:50:14.050 --> 00:50:15.050
What is it?

00:50:18.090 --> 00:50:19.090
I'm just going to walk her out.

00:50:20.460 --> 00:50:22.090
Jun Kyung, your clothes.

00:50:30.170 --> 00:50:33.540
Daniel, see you around.

00:50:41.410 --> 00:50:42.410
Hure.

00:50:43.910 --> 00:50:46.350
Sorry? What does that mean?

00:50:51.750 --> 00:50:52.950
It's nothing.

00:50:57.590 --> 00:50:58.630
Come on, let's go.

00:51:07.440 --> 00:51:09.070
I said I'd take you home.

00:51:09.140 --> 00:51:12.570
Who hires a designated driver just for a ride? I'm fine, really.

00:51:15.940 --> 00:51:18.950
What were you and Daniel talking about earlier?

00:51:23.890 --> 00:51:24.890
It's a secret.

00:51:29.090 --> 00:51:30.260
You have no idea.

00:51:31.230 --> 00:51:32.230
About what?

00:51:35.530 --> 00:51:38.470
Just how nervous I was.

00:51:42.440 --> 00:51:45.540
I only just became a dad out of the blue.

00:51:47.880 --> 00:51:49.410
And then introducing my girlfriend...

00:51:51.380 --> 00:51:54.220
to the son who just popped into my life.

00:51:58.890 --> 00:52:00.460
You made a real effort,

00:52:01.520 --> 00:52:03.360
and I'm so grateful for that.

00:52:07.900 --> 00:52:10.870
- It's here. - It's here.

00:52:38.590 --> 00:52:40.730
- Here you go. - This looks amazing.

00:52:41.330 --> 00:52:42.630
Thank you for the meal.

00:52:47.240 --> 00:52:48.240
So? What do you think?

00:52:48.940 --> 00:52:50.270
You were right, this place is great.

00:52:51.170 --> 00:52:53.340
- It's so delicious. - That's a relief.

00:52:56.510 --> 00:52:58.150
Ja Yeong, try the rolled omelet.

00:53:05.650 --> 00:53:08.760
This is so good. How are you such an amazing cook?

00:53:18.770 --> 00:53:21.700
Why are you looking at me like that? You're making me blush.

00:53:23.240 --> 00:53:24.240
Because you're beautiful.

00:53:25.140 --> 00:53:27.780
Because you look so beautiful, enjoying the food I made for you.

00:53:40.660 --> 00:53:42.060
It's fine, sir.

00:53:45.890 --> 00:53:47.330
Of course. Yes.

00:53:47.960 --> 00:53:48.960
Right.

00:53:49.500 --> 00:53:50.670
Okay, take care.

00:53:54.000 --> 00:53:57.270
They said the sports center won't pay until next week.

00:54:03.110 --> 00:54:06.110
See? This is why you don't deliver before you get paid. Right?

00:54:07.180 --> 00:54:08.180
People these days.

00:54:09.080 --> 00:54:10.920
You'd think there'd be some trust, you know?

00:54:15.690 --> 00:54:18.190
They'll probably pay eventually.

00:54:20.260 --> 00:54:22.430
They wouldn't just stiff us, would they?

00:54:22.900 --> 00:54:26.070
Yes, who would stiff us over that? They'll pay.

00:54:29.070 --> 00:54:30.070
So, what's on your mind?

00:54:32.070 --> 00:54:35.710
Even when I'm lost in my worries about making ends meet,

00:54:35.810 --> 00:54:38.310
I start worrying if Jin Ho is eating properly,

00:54:38.950 --> 00:54:41.750
and I worry he might suddenly get sick all by himself.

00:54:43.520 --> 00:54:45.820
Gosh, it just breaks my heart.

00:54:53.460 --> 00:54:56.200
You're back. You said you were craving meat.

00:54:56.830 --> 00:54:58.270
So I bought a ton of pork belly.

00:55:02.370 --> 00:55:03.370
Check this out.

00:55:06.310 --> 00:55:07.710
Hey, why haven't you been answering your phone?

00:55:08.610 --> 00:55:10.410
I had some really great news today.

00:55:11.280 --> 00:55:12.410
You're not going to believe it.

00:55:15.520 --> 00:55:16.520
Jun Seo.

00:55:17.450 --> 00:55:20.060
I was with Beom Jun.

00:55:21.060 --> 00:55:24.090
Whatever. I don't get jealous over stuff like that anymore, okay?

00:55:24.330 --> 00:55:25.990
I'm not jealous one bit. Seriously, not at all.

00:55:26.730 --> 00:55:28.730
Hurry up and wash up. I'll have this ready for you.

00:55:39.640 --> 00:55:41.240
I slept with Beom Jun.

00:56:11.910 --> 00:56:12.910
Gosh.

00:56:15.280 --> 00:56:17.780
Six, five, two, seven.

00:56:21.050 --> 00:56:22.549
Here. I'll be back...

00:56:22.550 --> 00:56:24.490
- after putting this in the fridge. - Okay.

00:56:34.700 --> 00:56:38.470
- Stop it. I'll do it. - No, it's fine.

00:56:39.200 --> 00:56:40.200
Goodness.

00:56:48.980 --> 00:56:49.980
Mi Kyung.

00:57:13.640 --> 00:57:14.640
Hure.

00:57:28.050 --> 00:57:31.120
(Hure in German)

00:57:39.490 --> 00:57:40.760
There are moments in life.

00:57:44.000 --> 00:57:45.930
Jin Ho, you weren't answering your phone.

00:57:46.400 --> 00:57:48.540
- So incredibly sudden... - Who are you?

00:57:51.610 --> 00:57:52.870
And impossible to escape.

00:58:00.750 --> 00:58:02.050
What did you just say?

00:58:05.050 --> 00:58:06.050
I'm sorry.

00:58:09.020 --> 00:58:10.590
Impossible to understand...

00:58:12.560 --> 00:58:14.060
and impossible to accept.

00:58:15.730 --> 00:58:16.800
Sorry for what?

00:58:18.270 --> 00:58:20.340
Just bleak and endless.

00:58:21.870 --> 00:58:23.840
I'm sorry I couldn't tell you sooner.

00:58:26.610 --> 00:58:29.139
(Hure: Prostitute)

00:58:29.140 --> 00:58:30.850
When things are utterly out of your control.

00:58:33.380 --> 00:58:35.150
Just one of those wretched moments.

00:58:39.750 --> 00:58:41.160
I asked who you were!

00:58:44.360 --> 00:58:46.190
That all-too-familiar moment...

00:58:55.200 --> 00:58:56.800
had found me once again.

00:59:02.010 --> 00:59:05.250
(Love Me)